1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,552
Continue your Windows command-line work from Android with TermLink.

2
00:00:04,562 --> 00:00:08,255
Both screens show a real, shared terminal session.

3
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:12,948
Windows Terminal is running PowerShell 7 on the PC.

4
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:17,413
Android connects to that same session for remote input and output.

5
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:20,344
First, Codex.

6
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:22,382
Type hi on Android.

7
00:00:22,392 --> 00:00:27,882
The CLI sends the request from Windows, and the reply appears on both screens.

8
00:00:27,892 --> 00:00:33,447
This is the running terminal interface, including its input box and Chinese text.

9
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,228
Next, launch Claude Code in the same PowerShell session.

10
00:00:38,238 --> 00:00:41,452
Send hi and watch the real reply arrive.

11
00:00:41,462 --> 00:00:46,018
TermLink keeps its interactive terminal interface visible on Android.

12
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:52,319
Now switch to OpenCode and send hi in its terminal interface.

13
00:00:52,329 --> 00:00:55,344
All three tools run on the Windows PC.

14
00:00:55,354 --> 00:00:58,397
Android provides remote input and viewing.

15
00:01:02,233 --> 00:01:05,973
Open the session menu to fit the terminal to the phone window.

16
00:01:05,983 --> 00:01:12,188
The keyboard, Enter key, and arrow keys are grouped at the bottom for interactive
command-line work.

17
00:01:12,967 --> 00:01:17,057
The computer keeps running while you check and control it from your phone.

18
00:01:17,067 --> 00:01:21,822
TermLink puts your remote command line and interactive tools in your pocket.
